\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Nana\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"48.01\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Nana\",\"delta\":\"+0.50%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"2.73\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"5.75\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-[3px]\",\"style\":{\"background\":\"linear-gradient(to bottom, #f59e0b, #f59e0b33)\",\"boxShadow\":\"0 0 12px -2px #f59e0b80\"}}],\"$La3\",\"$La4\"]}],\"$La5\",\"$La6\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"It is always about where you drop Molina\"]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Most Nana players treat Molina Smooch as a reactive tool: someone jumps the carry, throw Molina at where they landed. That version misses more than it lands. Molina drops at a location, then seeks and chases the nearest enemy hero in the area. By the time an assassin has already dived, they are already past the drop point.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The correct mental model: Molina Smooch is pre-placed, not thrown. Drop it at the bush entrance before the enemy jungler starts their rotation. Drop it at the Lithowanderer position before a contest. Drop it at your marksman's feet 3 seconds before you expect a dive. Molina that is waiting when the enemy arrives almost always lands. Molina thrown at someone already moving away almost never does.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"At max rank, Molina Smooch's cooldown is short enough that you can cycle Molina nearly continuously through a late-game teamfight. The value is not in landing one perfect transformation per fight. It is in having a Molina stationed somewhere useful at almost all times.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The secondary effect that gets underrated: every Molina hit reduces the target's magic defense for the duration. When your team sees Molina land, every magic dealer on your side has a window of amplified damage on that target. Ping the transformed hero immediately and let your team push through it.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first 8 minutes\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Level 1, take S1 and clear to the wall.\"}],\" Magic Boomerang hits on the way out and on the return, so a shallow pass through the wave catches the full line twice. Stand at the edge of wave range and angle the throw so the return arc passes through stragglers. Do not take S2 at level 1 without a target to pre-place it on: it costs mana and provides nothing for solo wave management.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Level 2, take S2 and move toward the river bush.\"}],\" Before the second wave reaches your tower, drop Molina in the bush nearest the enemy mid. If the enemy comes to contest the first Lithowanderer, Molina is already seeking. This forces them to forfeit the creep or get tagged. Many players keep walking because they do not see Molina waiting in the brush.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Level 4, consolidate mana before rotating.\"}],\" S1's mana cost climbs at every rank, and spamming S1 into the wave twice per wave will leave you dry by the time you are level 4. Hit the wave once cleanly per rotation, and wait until Enchanted Talisman is finished before treating mana as renewable. Your first rotation to assist the jungler or side lane should come after that item, not before.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The eight-minute power window\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Enchanted Talisman plus Genius Wand. Both items should be in your inventory by the 8-9 minute mark on mid lane, a minute or two later as roamer.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Enchanted Talisman solves both of Nana's early problems at once: the CDR brings S2 off cooldown faster, and the Mana Spring passive restores mana in the background so you stop going dry mid-rotation. With this item alone, Molina Smooch cycles fast enough that you are never caught without one ready when a fight finds you.\"}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Genius Wand stacks magic defense reduction per skill hit on enemy heroes, up to 3 stacks. Combined with Molina Smooch's own magic defense reduction on the tagged target, you are stripping resistance from two directions simultaneously. The enemy tank with 80 magic defense takes meaningfully more damage from everything your team throws at them than their stat screen suggests.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Before this two-item combination, Nana is a poke tool. After it, she is a fight starter.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Where to stand, and what you are aiming at\"]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The common reflex is to treat Nana as a backline caster: maximum range, throw S1 into the fight, and hope Molina finds someone. That pattern produces a low S2 hit rate because Molina's seek window expires against anyone already in motion at the moment of contact.\"}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three rules for positioning in teamfights:\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-1\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Position at mid-range, not max range.\"}],\" Molina needs to reach the target area, land, and seek the nearest enemy within chase distance. From maximum range you are dropping Molina on a position the enemy has already moved out of. From mid-range you can place it just ahead of where they will be when they reach your carry.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Ult into a CCed target, not a moving one.\"}],\" Molina Blitz fires three Molinas at the target area. The stun requires hitting any hero twice. Against a running target the three strikes land in different positions. Against an Atlas-locked or Tigreal-knocked-up cluster, all three overlap and the stun fires. Wait for your tank's CC before pressing your ultimate.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Use Molina's Gift to escape, not to re-engage.\"}],\" When the passive triggers, you are untargetable and gain a large movement speed bonus for the duration. The instinct is to turn and fight. Do not. The passive is on a long cooldown, so burning the window on a counter that fails leaves you with no out and a long stretch of vulnerable Nana. Use the window to reach your team or a turret.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-14\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The edge case: if your support is Estes or Angela, position one tier closer than you otherwise would. Sustained healing lets you absorb a poke hit and stay in position rather than retreating, which directly improves Molina placement accuracy.\"}]\n8f:[\"$\",\"$La7\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n90:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: three locked slots, three conversations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three items are fixed regardless of enemy composition: Arcane Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Genius Wand. The order is boots first, then Talisman, then Genius Wand. Playing roamer: swap Arcane Boots for Demon Boots and take the Encourage enchant, which hands nearby allies bonus magic power that scales with your roam gold plus a flat attack-speed share, worth more to the team than the flat magic penetration you give up.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The remaining three slots are situational:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",\"ul-0\",{\"className\":\"list-disc list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Glowing Wand\"}],\" when the enemy team has meaningful healing or sustain (Estes, Esmeralda, Uranus, Diggie). The Burn passive deals 1.5% of the target's max HP per second, and the Lifebane component cuts their healing by 50% for 3 seconds on hit. This handles anti-sustain without requiring a dedicated anti-heal item.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Ice Queen Wand\"}],\" when you want sustained slowing pressure across rotations. The slow stacks per skill hit and the spell vamp provides recovery through repeated trading. Better when you are already ahead and dictating the pace of fights.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Lightning Truncheon\"}],\" when you are the primary mage and not roaming. Every 6 seconds, your next skill chains additional magic damage to up to 3 nearby enemies. With S1's short cooldown you will trigger this passive regularly. Particularly strong against compositions that group up.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Holy Crystal\"}],\" when the game extends past 15 minutes and you have not built it yet. Pure scaling: extra magic power percentage that increases with hero level. Buy it fifth or sixth, not fourth. At the fourth slot you still have two items left, and Glowing Wand or Ice Queen Wand provide more practical value than raw scaling at that stage of the game.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Divine Glaive\"}],\" against enemies who are actively stacking magic defense (Athena's Shield plus Radiant Armor on the same target). The Spellbreaker passive converts their own magic defense into additional magic penetration for you, up to 20% extra. Against average compositions, Genius Wand's stacking handles enough. Only build this when a specific tank is becoming unkillable.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[\"$La8\",\"Five mistakes that lose Nana games\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\"]\n91:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Nana\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"92:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_d974ac796678180ff8724b88e192898b.png\",\"alt\":\"Atlas - Ocean Gladiator\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgZmlsbD0iIzBkMTIyNSIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex-1 min-w-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading font-bold text-text-primary group-hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors truncate\",\"children\":\"Atlas\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex